From f9013de5c0dcdbfac41e79c586f7192f253c0cc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:05:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dflash: a rejected draft checkpoint image must not kill the
 server process

Ports the portable half of buun's e332b2494 "dflash: harden checkpoint rewind lifecycle" and
records the buun review wave the 2026-08-27 deep review chartered.

WHAT LANDED. common_prompt_checkpoint::try_load_dft - a non-aborting variant of load_dft. Our tree
has four load_dft call sites; three are prompt/spec-checkpoint restores in server-context.cpp and
every one of them reached GGML_ABORT("checkpoint size mismatch") on an incompatible draft image,
i.e. an ill-formed restore killed the whole server. Those three now reject the image, warn, clear
the drafter sequence, and continue; ordinary prefill rebuilds it.

CONSERVATIVE DEVIATION, deliberate: buun's rewrite makes load_dft(ctx == nullptr) with a non-empty
image an abort. Ours keeps the pre-existing no-op for a null context - only try_load_dft treats a
missing context as a rejection. One previously un-guarded call site would otherwise have gained a
new abort path.

WHAT WAS NOT TAKEN, and why. common_speculative_sequence_event / _sequence_transition and both impl
overrides mutate buun-only drafter state (stash, positions[].target_base, adpt, pregate_*,
seq_in_gen, proposals, carry_rows_per_seq, common_speculative_impl_dflash::ring_state_reset). Grep
over our common/speculative.cpp: zero hits for all of them - our draft_dflash impl is the PR-27342 +
0394/0397 lineage with a dflash2_adpt controller instead. The enum alone would be a dispatcher with
no overrides and no callers. The cross-ring-interleave.cu leg is CUDA, off-rig.

THE OTHER THREE TAKEs ARE SKIPPED on the defect-presence check the deep review itself listed as
owed, each shown rather than assumed:
  2714303b5 - defect ABSENT. Its HTTP-500 fix lives in buun's target_base/dft_pos0 rebase
              machinery; our tree has neither symbol (Grep over common/: 0 hits).
  92eef392a - substrate ABSENT. It repairs buun's mmproj-GPU-swap fit solver; none of
              mmproj_gpu_swap / swap_fit_solved / n_ctx_fit / hp_nct_mtp / n_seq_max_full exists
              in our server-context.cpp.
  9d0d4b650 - VBR-only, and the review's "no VBR symbols" claim is refuted: the 54 lines use
              vbr_params_, vbr_layer_policy, cpu_bound_kv, try_vmm_alloc, ggml_type_is_turbo, and
              our src/llama-kv-cache.cpp has none of them.

REGISTER WORK. licenses/buun-MIT.txt did not exist while buun-derived code (series patch 0394,
2026-08-21) was already on arifi/main - retained verbatim and rowed in licenses/README.md. Two
sources.json rows added, neither moving the pin: the 0394 ingestion backfill the review filed as
owed, and this wave. buun stays pinned at 39d97a876; the 70-commit VBR CONFLICT bucket stands.

CONSERVATISM PROOF: git diff --numstat arifi/main..HEAD over ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/*, *vulkan*,
*.comp and ggml/include/ggml.h is EMPTY - the F-138 reorder fix and the TQ3/TURBO id block are
untouched.

BUILD: compiled and archived clean (libserver-context.a, libllama-server-impl.a, libllama-common.a
relinked 2026-08-27 20:01-20:02); llama-cli/llama-quantize/test-backend-ops/test-quantize-fns exes
relinked 20:03-20:04. llama-server.exe could NOT be relinked - a live server process (PID 22172,
started 19:17) holds the file; it was deliberately NOT killed.

Taken-from: github.com/spiritbuun/buun-llama-cpp@e332b2494
Origin: ArifiLabs - portable half only, re-derived against our server; see body for the declined half
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED (no benchmark arm; the guard replaces a process abort on a path that needs a mismatched draft image to reach)
